Integrating these targets into instruments such as National Waste Management Plans with clear implementation plans is essential to show commitment and align with NDCs. Many countries mention methane in their NDCs, but few set quantified targets for methane emissions from the waste sector. Best examples include:

- Colombia: reduction of methane emissions from waste fully integrated into national climate strategies;

- Indonesia: quantifies wastewater measures equal to 1.2 Mt of methane recovery;

- Viet Nam: commitments to methane capture from wastewater treatment plants.

